      "text": "Perform faithful manga colorization on the first input page. Change color only in the existing artwork; do not redesign, reconstruct, beautify, denoise, sharpen or add detail. The first input image is the absolute authority for pixels and geometry. Preserve every panel border, crop, line, screentone pattern, face, eye, mouth, expression, pose, silhouette, hand, prop, background object and whitespace in exactly the same position and shape. Speech bubbles, caption boxes and sound-effect regions are locked source regions: keep their white backgrounds and copy every glyph, punctuation mark, numeral, letter, stroke, spacing and line break exactly; leave all text pure black and white. Use the reference images only to choose colors for characters already visible, never to change identity or anatomy. Apply clean professional anime cel colors with coherent character palettes, natural skin tones, saturated but balanced hair and clothing, smooth flat fills, restrained shading and clean backgrounds. This is colorization only; output the same page, not a redraw.",
      "clip": ["6", 0]
    },
    "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
    "_meta": {"title": "Colorization Instruction"}
  },
  "9": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "redraw, repaint, reconstruction, beautification, denoise, sharpening, invented detail, new content, removed content, altered face, altered anatomy, altered pose, changed background, changed crop, warped line art, enhanced screentone, hallucinated pattern, colored text, rewritten text, translated text, missing glyph, changed punctuation, changed typography, gray cast, desaturated color, washed-out color, overexposure, color noise, watermark, logo",
